1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,680
Hello, I'm DiGi. This one's for you and your grown up.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,240
Snuggle up. Ready?

3
00:00:07,433 --> 00:00:11,837
Before we start, let's do our big breath.

4
00:00:11,837 --> 00:00:14,875
Breathe in, and out.

5
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:16,835
Lovely.

6
00:00:16,985 --> 00:00:19,225
Remember our last adventure?

7
00:00:19,225 --> 00:00:24,865
A picture on a screen shows only a little. Can you say it?

8
00:00:25,085 --> 00:00:29,219
That's it. Screen me is a little slice.

9
00:00:29,219 --> 00:00:31,280
Real me is the whole me.

10
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:34,686
Today we take one more step.

11
00:00:34,866 --> 00:00:37,077
Today we learn one big thing.

12
00:00:37,077 --> 00:00:40,746
Some things on screens are pretend.

13
00:00:40,746 --> 00:00:44,845
Pretend means made up, like a story.

14
00:00:45,079 --> 00:00:48,659
Say our special word. Pretend.

15
00:00:48,659 --> 00:00:52,107
Look at these two dogs. One dog is a cartoon.

16
00:00:52,107 --> 00:00:56,826
He can talk, and drive a car, and fly to the moon.

17
00:00:56,826 --> 00:00:59,260
The other dog is a real dog.

18
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:03,506
He can bark, and run, and lick your face.

19
00:01:03,506 --> 00:01:07,959
One of them is real, and one of them is pretend.

20
00:01:08,139 --> 00:01:12,272
Pretend means someone made it up, like a story.

21
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:16,506
And guess what? Pretend is fun.

22
00:01:16,506 --> 00:01:20,503
Cartoons, stories, superheroes, magic.

23
00:01:20,503 --> 00:01:23,186
We love pretend.

24
00:01:23,486 --> 00:01:26,626
And here's a little secret about me.

25
00:01:26,626 --> 00:01:29,246
I'm pretend too. I'm a cartoon.

26
00:01:29,246 --> 00:01:31,926
I'm not a real person.

27
00:01:31,926 --> 00:01:36,389
But I always tell you the truth about it. That's our deal.

28
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:40,790
Real means it is really, truly happening.

29
00:01:40,963 --> 00:01:42,830
And here's the tricky bit.

30
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:48,283
On screens, some things are real, and some things are pretend.

31
00:01:48,543 --> 00:01:51,981
Even a video with real people in it can be made up.

32
00:01:51,981 --> 00:01:55,543
Even grown ups have to stop and think.

33
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:57,990
Pause me here. And grown up,

34
00:01:57,990 --> 00:02:00,488
ask your little one:

35
00:02:00,488 --> 00:02:03,350
can you think of something on a screen that's pretend,

36
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:05,728
and something that's real?

37
00:02:06,068 --> 00:02:07,710
I'll wait.

38
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,506
When something on a screen makes you go,

39
00:02:10,506 --> 00:02:13,394
"Ooh, is that really true?"

40
00:02:13,854 --> 00:02:17,117
That's the moment for our magic question.

41
00:02:17,117 --> 00:02:19,151
Is this real?

42
00:02:19,392 --> 00:02:21,304
And here's the very best part.

43
00:02:21,304 --> 00:02:25,058
You don't have to know the answer all by yourself.

44
00:02:25,058 --> 00:02:28,371
You have a helper. You have your grown up.

45
00:02:28,371 --> 00:02:31,658
Here's what that sounds like.

46
00:02:31,658 --> 00:02:33,154
A child might say,

47
00:02:33,154 --> 00:02:38,473
"This video says if I don't share it, something bad will happen.

48
00:02:38,473 --> 00:02:40,536
Is that real?"

49
00:02:40,536 --> 00:02:43,871
And the grown up says, "Ooh, good question.

50
00:02:43,871 --> 00:02:46,576
Let's think together."

51
00:02:46,976 --> 00:02:50,466
"No. That one is made up. Nothing bad will happen.

52
00:02:50,466 --> 00:02:53,110
You were so clever to ask me."

53
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:56,748
See? Asking is the clever thing to do.

54
00:02:56,748 --> 00:03:00,430
Asking is being a detective.

55
00:03:00,743 --> 00:03:03,687
Grown up, this one's yours.

56
00:03:03,687 --> 00:03:07,210
Pause me. Say it together:

57
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:09,937
"When we are not sure, we ask."

58
00:03:09,937 --> 00:03:13,043
Then a great big high five.

59
00:03:13,043 --> 00:03:18,263
Now our magic question, three times. Big voices!

60
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:21,065
Is this real?

61
00:03:21,126 --> 00:03:23,250
Is this real?

62
00:03:23,392 --> 00:03:25,426
Is this real?

63
00:03:25,426 --> 00:03:28,362
Tonight, play the real or pretend game.

64
00:03:28,362 --> 00:03:30,922
Watch a little something together.

65
00:03:30,922 --> 00:03:33,796
A cartoon, a video, anything.

66
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:37,924
Every so often, your grown up says, "Real or pretend?"

67
00:03:37,924 --> 00:03:41,596
And you point and shout your answer.

68
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:44,236
Real dog? Pretend dragon?

69
00:03:44,236 --> 00:03:47,629
Real rain? Pretend magic?

70
00:03:47,629 --> 00:03:49,020
It's a giggly little game.

71
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:52,427
And you're learning to be a screen detective.

72
00:03:52,662 --> 00:03:58,393
Before I go, show your grown up one thing you remember from today.

73
00:03:58,393 --> 00:04:00,496
Anything at all.

74
00:04:00,496 --> 00:04:03,462
Got it? Brilliant.

75
00:04:03,462 --> 00:04:06,280
Remember, screens are better together.

76
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,614
See you next time.
